><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9183978-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9183978</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> </patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1055714A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURAOKA HITOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKISUI CHEMICAL COMPANY LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TONO MASAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURAOKA, HITOMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKISUI CHEMICAL COMPANY, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TONO, MASAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURAOKA HITOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TONO MASAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURAOKA, HITOMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TONO, MASAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A fire-resistant coating material comprising an epoxy resin, a hardener, and an inorganic filler or comprising a butyl or isobutylene rubber and an inorganic filler, wherein (1) the sum of the epoxy resin and the hardener or the amount of the butyl or isobutylene rubber is 100 parts by weight, (2) the amount of the inorganic filler, comprising a neutralized, heat-expandable graphite, etc., is 200 to 500 parts by weight, (3) the amount of the neutralized, heat-expandable graphite in the inorganic filler is 15 to 400 parts by weight, (4) and the fire-resistant coating material has a viscosity as measured with a Brookfield viscometer of 1 to 1,000 P. The coating material has remarkable fire resistance and is usable in a wide range of applications.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un matériau de revêtement résistant au feu contenant une résine époxyde, un durcissant, et une charge inorganique, ou contenant du butyle ou du caoutchouc d'isobutylène et une charge inorganique; matériau dans lequel: (1) la somme de la résine époxyde et du durcissant ou la quantité du butyle ou du caoutchouc d'isobutylène représente 100 parties en poids, (2) la quantité de la charge inorganique, comprenant un graphite neutralisé thermoexpansible, etc., représente entre 200 et 500 parties en poids, (3) la quantité du graphite neutralisé thermoexpansible dans la charge inorganique représente entre 15 et 400 parties en poids, et enfin, (4) le matériau de revêtement résistant au feu présente une viscosité telle que mesurée avec un viscosimètre Brookfield, se situant entre 1 et 1000 P. En outre, ce matériau de revêtement est hautement résistant au feu et peut être utilisé dans une grande variété d'applications.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>